= Liquidity provider — Simple =

A liquidity provider supplies assets so a market or protocol has inventory available for other users. In AMMs, providers often earn fees, but they also take risks from price changes, trading against better-informed participants, software, and the market design.

'''Important boundary:''' liquidity provider ≠ trader by identity.

